F_CL to F_total when DynamicCLMode > 1.5 (Stage 15C write path).

DESIGN (meets the 6-item review checklist):
  1. Mode=1 (DynamicCLMode<=1) is UNCHANGED: the only new executable line is
     `if (DynamicCLMode > 1.5) { F_total[...] += fcl_...; }`, which is dead at
     Mode=1. calcDynamicCLShadow still runs for diagnostics, as in 15B.
  2. F_CL is added EXACTLY ONCE per F_total assembly, in the force-iteration
     loop (MRT) and once per BGK force update. No second add elsewhere.
  3. MRT and BGK paths are symmetric: identical hoist + identical guarded add.
  4. NO double scaling: calcDynamicCLShadow already returns the FULLY scaled,
     capped force vector (mag = ForceSign*Coeff*(sigma/IntWidth)*R_theta*I_cl,
     capped at ForceCap*sigma/IntWidth, then *t_CL). The caller adds it raw.
  5. PhaseF / gradPhi / mu / WallGhost are NOT touched. F_CL only enters F_total.
  6. Force cap is preserved (applied inside calcDynamicCLShadow, untouched).
     Diagnostics (ForceCandidate*, CosResidual, Active, ...) are still written
     by calcDynamicCLShadow on every call, Mode-independent.

This is DIFF-ONLY. Do NOT compile, run, or commit until reviewed and authorised.

